course: dictionary
lesson: 8201
title: Resuscitation: bringing life back
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Resuscitation is a noun. It means bringing someone back to life or to consciousness when their heart or breathing has stopped. Its short name is CPR, which stands for cardiopulmonary resuscitation.
explain: Context clues help you here. «CPR, cardiopulmonary resuscitation, means pressing hard and fast on the middle of the chest to keep blood moving when the heart has stopped.» The words heart has stopped and keep blood moving tell you this is about saving a life.
explain: The word has a second meaning too: bringing an idea, plan or business back into use. Read the sentence around it. If a plan has been lying unused for years and is now being restarted, resuscitation fits. When you are unsure, swap in your meaning and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Resuscitation means bringing someone back to life or consciousness when their heart or breathing has stopped.
fact: «CPR» means cardiopulmonary resuscitation, and it is the life-saving help you can learn in first aid lessons.
fact: In an emergency, call the emergency number, such as 999 in the UK, 911 in the USA, or 000 in Australia, and press hard and fast in the middle of the chest.
fact: «Resus» is the name for the emergency room in hospital dramas.
fact: Resuscitation can also mean bringing an idea, plan or business back into use.
exercise: «CPR, cardiopulmonary resuscitation, means pressing hard and fast on the middle of the chest.» In this sentence, what is resuscitation most like? | A kind of dance | A type of cold drink | *Life-saving help for someone whose heart has stopped | A game played with a ball
exercise: In the UK, which is the emergency number you call? | *999 | 123 | 000 | 911
exercise: In hospital dramas, «Resus» is the name for what? | A kitchen | A school sports hall | The car park | *The emergency room
test: Find and copy the phrase from «CPR, cardiopulmonary resuscitation, means pressing hard and fast on the middle of the chest to keep blood moving when the heart has stopped.» that tells you when CPR is needed. | *when the heart has stopped | to keep blood moving | pressing hard and fast | the middle of the chest
test: Which sentence uses resuscitation to mean bringing a plan back into use? | The doctor began resuscitation on the man at once. | *After years on the shelf, the old library plan got a resuscitation. | The nurse called for resuscitation equipment. | The children had a resuscitation of their football at break.
exam: Jayden says resuscitation is only a hospital word. Why is he only partly right? | It is a type of sport played on grass | It is only a kind of medicine taken by mouth | *It is also first aid, like CPR, and it can mean bringing a plan back into use | It means a very loud shout
